  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced`, but I kept `totalCents` and `placedAt` instead of renaming. I haven't run `npm test`, `npm run arch` or the typecheck. The shell was denied approval, and the session has no way to approve it.\n\nI kept the old fields because ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event. A straight rename would break them, and renames have to go through deprecation first.\n\n- **Event change:** `src/core/events.ts` now emits the new fields with the same values as the old ones. The old fields are marked `@deprecated`, and `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change is purely additive.\n- **Tests:** I updated the expected event in `test/app.test.ts` and added an `amountCents` check in `test/adapters.test.ts`.\n- **Unchanged:** the HTTP response from `GET /orders/{id}` and `POST /orders` still returns `placedAt` and `totalCents`. ARCH-8 requires it to stay backward compatible, and your request was about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, check that both consumers have moved to the new fields. After that, `totalCents` and `placedAt` can be removed from the event, which should come with a schema version bump.",
